#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""cardputer-mc: a MeshCore chat client for the M5 CardputerZero with the Cap-LoRa-1262 module.

One file. `cardputer-mc install` sets everything up once (apt packages, a venv, meshcore-pi,
a config with a fresh identity); `cardputer-mc` then starts meshcore-pi as a child process,
switches the module's 5V supply on, and runs the ncurses chat on top of it. Quitting stops
meshcore-pi and switches the 5V supply off again.

meshcore-pi (https://github.com/brianwiddas/meshcore-pi) drives the SX1262 over SPI and exposes
a MeshCore companion-radio interface on 127.0.0.1:5000; this client talks to it with the
`meshcore` Python library. The chat UI is derived from mcorechat.

State lives in ~/.local/share/cardputer-mc (override with CARDPUTER_MC_HOME):
  config.toml       radio settings, name and private key of this node (mode 600)
  meshcore-pi/      the pinned meshcore-pi checkout
  venv/             Python environment for both
  contacts.mesh, channels.json, meshcore.log, local-radio.log
Chat history and UI settings live in ~/.config/cardputer-mc.
"""

